Example 16 — `minimal` vs `extended` projection presets
=======================================================

This example demonstrates the two string presets accepted by
`PAOFLOW.projections(..., configuration=...)`:

  * `"minimal"`  — pseudo-atomic wavefunctions (`PP_PSWFC`) read
                   straight from each species' UPF.
  * `"extended"` — pure all-electron basis built from
                   `BASIS/<elem>/*.dat`: the same valence shells as
                   `"minimal"` augmented by a rule-based polarization
                   set (see `PAOFLOW/defs/basis_presets.py`).

Two subdirectories cover complementary regimes:

  Si_ONCV/  scalar-relativistic ONCV pseudo (insulator, fcc Si)
  Pt_REL/   fully-relativistic ultrasoft PSL pseudo (metal, fcc Pt,
            noncollinear + spin-orbit)

Manual / hand-written shell lists are NOT included here on purpose —
see example10 (GaAs) and example15 (Si ONCV) for that comparison.

Workflow in each subdirectory
-----------------------------
1) `pw.x < scf.in  > scf.out`
2) `pw.x < nscf.in > nscf.out`
3) `python main.py`

`main.py` is self-contained: it runs PAOFLOW twice (once per preset)
through the projections -> projectability -> pao_hamiltonian -> bands
pipeline and writes
    output_minimal/bands_0.dat
    output_extended/bands_0.dat
plus an overlay `bands_minimal_vs_extended.png` (matplotlib optional).

The path to `BASIS/` is auto-resolved from the repository layout; set
`PAOFLOW_BASISPATH` to override.

Reference bands (to be regenerated by the maintainer) live under
`<subdir>/Reference/`.
